  "body": "I deployed Matrix-synapse-py3 v1.78 by deb mode(not docker) in mainland China, but it cannot access the matrix.org notification push API. I configured the Proxy variable in the Ubuntu20.04 environment. When I Connect to https://matrix.org through wget curl, etc.,\r\n```\r\n< HTTP/2 405\r\n< date: Thu, 09 Mar 2023 17:06:30 GMT\r\n< content-type: text/html; charset=utf-8\r\n< allow: HEAD, POST\r\n< permissions-policy: interest-cohort=()\r\n< cf-cache-status: DYNAMIC\r\n< server: cloudflare\r\n< cf-ray: 7a54e8aa0bf4a7c3-ICN\r\n\r\n<html>\r\n  <head><title>405 - Method Not Allowed</title></head>\r\n  <body>\r\n    <h1>Method Not Allowed</h1>\r\n    <p>Your browser approached me (at /_matrix/push/v1/notify) with the method \"GET\".  I only allow the methods HEAD, POST here.</p>\r\n  </body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\nIt looks good but the push process is still blocked,and in the log file:\r\n```\r\nsynapse.http.client - 472 - INFO - httppush.process-10658 - Error sending request to POST https://matrix. org/_matrix/push/v1/notify: RequestTimedOutError 504: Timeout connecting to remote server\r\n```\r\nI checked the documentation of Synapse, it told me that the https_proxy variable is supported. \r\nMy proxy service is not on localhost, and the ip is not in \"url_preview_ip_range_blacklist\"\r\n\r\nIs there any way for me to connect to the Push API?",
